from pathlib import Path
import json
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;data=R/'data';summary=json.loads((data/'summary.json').read_text());histories=json.loads((data/'index.json').read_text())
text='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Five-parameter hot-gas cones</title><style>body{font:16px system-ui;max-width:1250px;margin:30px auto;padding:0 20px;background:#faf9f6;color:#202a32}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}td,th{border-bottom:1px solid #ccc;padding:9px;text-align:left}img{width:100%}select,input{font:inherit}section{background:white;padding:20px;margin:20px 0;border:1px solid #ddd;border-radius:8px}.note{color:#555}a{color:#136d8b}</style><h1>Can five values describe the hot gas?</h1><p>A geometric fit to 48 existing development histories, not a learned prediction or an ignition-risk model. No new simulation or training.</p><section><h2>What each frame contains</h2><p>Pivot height (m), tilt from vertical (degrees), axial length (m), end radius (m), and peak temperature inside the cone (°C). The apex stays on the tree centreline (x=8, y=8); horizontal direction is fixed to +x, the ambient wind direction. A null cone means no saved cells above 50°C.</p><p><b>Time:</b> values describe an instantaneous saved frame approximately every two seconds. They are not maxima over the intervening interval.</p><p><b>Boundary:</b> fit aims to capture at least 95% of cell centres above 50°C. This threshold is a diagnostic choice, not ignition. Peak temperature does not describe temperatures elsewhere in the cone; the fitted cone can miss the domain's hottest cell.</p></section><section><h2>Does the cone fit tightly?</h2>TABLE<p>Captured = fraction of hot cells inside the shape. Purity = fraction of enclosed cells that are hot. IoU = hot/shape intersection divided by their union. Frame medians are over active frames, not equal configuration weighting.</p><p>The original oval is a 2σ covariance summary. The equal-coverage ovoid retains its full 3-D centre/orientation/axis ratios and expands to capture 95% of hot cells; it has more geometric freedom than this cone, so this comparison does not isolate a single shape choice.</p><p><b>Finding:</b> forcing a pointed cone to enclose most hot gas often makes it too broad. Ground-level apex selections are geometric compromises, not evidence that combustion pivots there. No claim of a globally optimal cone is made.</p></section><section><h2>Inspect each history</h2><label>Case <select id="case"></select></label><p id="conditions"></p><img id="plot" alt="Saved temperature fields with cone and original oval overlays"><p>Fixed storyboard times are near 20, 40, 80 and 160 s. White triangle is the projected cone; magenta dashed ellipse is the original 2σ summary. Colours show maximum temperature through y, not a slice or visible flame. The full 3-D masks determine all numeric overlap scores.</p><label>Numeric frame <input id="time" type="range" min="0" max="90" value="20"></label><p id="frame"></p><table id="numbers"></table><p><a id="raw">Download full history JSON</a></p></section><section><h2>Scope and omissions</h2><p>Generic conical vegetation crowns 3 m wide and 4–10 m tall, starting 2 m above ground; 0.5 m cells in a 24×16×16 m domain. Artificial 1500°C igniter for the first 20 s. No trunks, buildings or embers. Hot gas includes the imposed igniter; it is not separated into tree-only combustion. No physical validation.</p><p>The fitted apex may be at ground level or at seven heights within the crown; tilt is searched in 10° increments. At most 1,024 hot cells rank candidates, then the best eight candidates are recalibrated on every hot cell. The smallest analytic cone volume among those candidates is selected. Geometry can extend outside the observed domain; overlap scores only describe the saved domain.</p><p>No incident heat flux, radiation outside the cone, within-interval temperature peak, or target ignition is inferred. The 48 histories are previously examined development data (8 train, 40 validation), not untouched tests.</p><p><a href="summary.json">Summary JSON</a> · <a href="https://github.com/davies-w/wildfire3d/tree/codex/ignition-surrogate-pilot/experiments/44_hot_gas_cones">Source and reproduction</a></p></section><script>const D=DATA;const q=id=>document.getElementById(id);D.forEach((c,i)=>{const o=document.createElement('option');o.value=i;o.textContent=c.case;q('case').append(o)});function frame(){const c=D[+q('case').value],r=c.snapshots[+q('time').value];q('frame').textContent=r.time_s.toFixed(3)+' seconds · '+(r.igniter_on?'igniter ON':'igniter OFF');q('numbers').innerHTML='<tr><th>Quantity</th><th>Value</th></tr>'+Object.entries({...r.cone,hot_capture:r.cone_metrics?.hot_recall,hot_purity:r.cone_metrics?.hot_precision,cone_iou:r.cone_metrics?.iou,ovoid95_iou:r.ovoid95_metrics?.iou,missed_peak_C:r.peak_temperature_missed_C}).map(([k,v])=>'<tr><td>'+k+'</td><td>'+(v==null?'No active cone':v.toFixed(4))+'</td></tr>').join('');}function draw(){const c=D[+q('case').value];q('conditions').textContent='Wind '+c.conditions.wind_speed+' m/s (+x); crown height '+c.conditions.crown_height_m+' m; '+c.conditions.split;q('plot').src='plots/'+c.case+'.png';q('raw').href='histories/'+c.case+'.json';frame()}q('case').onchange=draw;q('time').oninput=frame;draw();</script></html>'''
a=summary['active'];post=summary['after_igniter'];table='<table><tr><th>Shape</th><th>Median hot capture</th><th>Median purity</th><th>Median IoU</th></tr>'
for label,rec,prec,iou in [('Cone',a['cone_recall_median'],a['cone_precision_median'],a['cone_iou_median']),('Original 2σ ovoid',a['ovoid_recall_median'],None,a['ovoid_iou_median']),('Ovoid expanded to 95%',a['ovoid95_recall_median'],a['ovoid95_precision_median'],a['ovoid95_iou_median'])]:
 table+='<tr><td>'+label+'</td>'+''.join('<td>'+('—' if v is None else f'{v:.1%}')+'</td>' for v in [rec,prec,iou])+'</tr>'
table+=f"</table><p>{summary['snapshots']:,} saved frames; {a['frames']:,} contain gas above 50°C. Cone apex below crown in {a['apex_below_crown_fraction']:.1%} of active frames. Hottest domain cell missed in {a['peak_missed_frames']} frames. After the igniter is off, median cone purity is {post['cone_precision_median']:.1%}.</p>"
(data/'report.html').write_text(text.replace('TABLE',table).replace('DATA',json.dumps(histories)))
